a day to celebrate past russian  successes with old allies president  vladimir putin arrived at the vostochny  cosmodrome in russia's far east with  bella russian president alexander  lukashenko  to mark 61 years since one of the  biggest achievements in russia's history  april 12 1961 russian cosmonaut yuri  gagarin became the first man in space a  clearly happy memory for the president  who says he still remembers that day as  a nine-year-old boy but the ongoing  conflict with ukraine is still at the  top of the agenda for president putin  unfortunately ukraine was created as  some kind of launch pad for aggression  against russia and the offshoots of  nationalism were totally cherished this  new generation of ukrainian nationalists  are especially clashing with russia you  see how nazi ideology became a fact of  life in ukraine it was unavoidable we  are taking steps to provide security for  russia we didn't have any other choice  we did the right thing and i have no  doubt that our aims will be achieved  russia's so-called special military  operation is now in its second phase  which officials say will focus on the  dambass region of ukraine vladimir putin  also praised russian troops for what he  calls efficiently courageously and  competently carrying out their operation  that operation was a topic of  discussions between the russian  president and his bella russian  counterpart belarus has hosted russian  troops since earlier this year  and the kiev government accused minsk of  allowing their borders to be used by  russian troops to enter ukraine  despite the criticism from the west  president lukashenko's support for  vladimir putin continues to be  unwavering  prior to their meeting lukashenko vowed  belarus will always be by russia's side  the two presidents emerged from their  discussions with renewed determination  to consolidate their unity which will  include closer military ties  we discussed in detail important issues  including political diplomatic economic  and of course military and defense our  modern history hasn't seen yet such  dangerous and complicated moments in our  relationship with the west putin also  praised lukashenko's role in starting  the negotiations between moscow and kiev  which are still ongoing but the russian  president admitted that they have now  reached a deadlock those talks between  russian and ukrainian officials began  just a few days after russia's military  operation but there were never any high  hopes that they would bring an end to  the fighting anytime soon  now vladimir putin has confirmed what  many feared that this conflict will only  end once russia achieves its objectives  regardless of how long it takes and at  what cost  dorso jabari al jazeera moscow
 

